.TH QWSERVER 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwserver \- start high-concurrency local llama-server daemon for Qwen3-4B
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwserver
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIport\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fIextra flags...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwserver
spawns the high-throughput \fBllama\-server\fR background process, exposing an OpenAI-compatible HTTP API and Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming endpoint.
All terminal tools (\fBqwfile\fR, \fBqwsec\fR, \fBqwpipe\fR, \fBqwcli\fR) detect and route queries through this server automatically when active.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " tokens"
Allocate context window size (16, 32, or 48 thousand tokens). Default is 32.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
TCP port to bind the HTTP server to. Default is 8080.
.TP
.BI \-r " level"
Set reasoning effort profile (\fI0\fR to \fI4\fR). Default is 2.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the server with 48k context on port 8080:
.RS
.nf
qwserver \-c 48 \-p 8080
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qwfile (1),
.BR qwcli (1),
